          "bank": [
            {
              "task": "free-text-round-trip-5-1",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "A value-taking flag whose value is exactly `--` became unwritable, leaving a new hole in §2.2 byte-identity bar that no command can now close.",
              "failure": "An agent reads a task whose description is exactly `--` out of `tick show` and writes it back with `tick update <id> --description --`; the marker is consumed by parseArgs and the command fails with `Error: --description requires a value` (verified against the working tree; before this change the same invocation stored the two-dash description). Noticed by the phase own round-trip fixture task (free-text-round-trip-5-5, The Awkward-Task Fixture Round-Trips Byte-Identically) if it covers a dash-only value, otherwise by a user whose text is silently unwritable. Task 5-2 split does not fix it — post-marker arguments become positionals, so the value can never re-attach to --description.",
              "detail": "Marker recognition at internal/cli/app.go:374-377 consumes a bare `--` wherever it appears, including the slot a value-taking flag value occupies; the parsers that then find no value are parseCreateArgs (internal/cli/create.go:46-51), parseUpdateArgs, parseListFlags and parseShowArgs. The same family already exists pre-existing for values that spell a global flag (`--description --json` fails today because applyGlobalFlag strips the value at any position), which is why a fix belongs at the phase level rather than in either task: supporting the `--flag=value` form for value-taking flags closes both at once. The task body accepts this as its single documented regression.",
              "files": [
                "internal/cli/app.go",
                "internal/cli/create.go",
                "internal/cli/update.go",
                "internal/cli/list.go",
                "internal/cli/show.go"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "free-text-round-trip-5-2",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "`migrate` is the one command still reading post-marker text as flags; the literal split is per-handler opt-in with nothing enforcing it.",
              "failure": "`tick migrate --from beads -- --dry-run` performs a dry run — verified, the output carries [dry-run]. The marker is silently ignored, so once the README task publishes \"`--` means everything after it is text\", a caller who follows that rule on migrate gets a no-op import and only notices when the tasks they expected are absent. The same hole reopens for any command added later: forgetting fc.SplitLiterals in a new handler produces no compile error and no test failure.",
              "detail": "parseMigrateArgs (internal/cli/migrate.go:46-65) scans all of args for --from/--dry-run/--pending-only, and App.Run passes the unsplit subArgs to a.handleMigrate(subArgs) (internal/cli/app.go:82) one line after it has already computed migrateFlagArgs for ValidateFlags (internal/cli/app.go:79) — so the split half exists and is discarded. Two shapes for the consolidation pass: (a) convert parseMigrateArgs like its siblings (two lines; migrate has no positional so literals are simply dropped as list drops them); (b) the structural fix — split once in App.Run and hand both halves to every handler, so a handler cannot forget. (b) reaches every handler signature, which is why it belongs at the phase boundary.",
              "files": [
                "internal/cli/migrate.go",
                "internal/cli/app.go"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
